---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_95",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 95,
  "text": "<p> [[255.1]] <b>81. HEINRICH OLDENBURG AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[255.2]] London, 28. September (8. Oktober) 1671. [73.86.]</b></p>\n<p> [[255.15]] Ampliss^#'o et Consultiss^#'o Viro </p>\n<p> [[255.16]] Dⁿ^#'o Goth. Guil. Leibnitio J.U.D. et Consil. Moguntino </p>\n<p> [[255.17]] Henr. Oldenburg Sal. </p>\n<p> [[255.18]] Tardius aliquanto binis tuis novissimis, 18. junii et 20. ejusdem ad me datis, respondeo,\n[[255.19]] quod rusticari ad tempus, deinde complura negotia, nullam ferentia moram, expedire debuerim. </p>\n<p> [[255.20]] Gaudeo interim, quae antehac ad [Schultzium] Hamburgensem in usum tuum transmisi,\n[[255.21]] rite Tibi dudum fuisse reddita. Ex eo tempore, <b>Numero</b> 74. <i>Ephemeridum</i> mearum <i>Philosophicarum</i>,\n[[255.22]] Doctoris Wallisii de <i>Hypothesi</i> tua <i>Physica</i> judicium inserui, quem libellum ab\n[[255.23]] eodem bibliopola Hamburgensi ad Te curatum quoque fuisse plane confido. </p>\n<p> [[255.24]] Caeterum <Fn><i>Neben dem Absatz von Leibniz Hand:</i> NB</Fn> quod artem illam attinet, quam Amicum tuum callere scribis, Chalybem scil. ex\n[[255.25]] ferro in quantitate cum magno emolumento parandi, scire te velim, Serenissimum Principem\n[[256.1]] Rupertum Palatinum hic Londini artificium illud perquam facili negotio in praxin deduxisse, et\n[[256.2]] quoties lubet deducere. Quaevis enim Instrumenta ferrea, penitus jam confecta, integra etiam\n[[256.3]] tormenta bellica grandia aeque ac parva, etc. novit Ille in Chalybem perfectum, multo minori\n[[256.4]] quam secus fit sumptu, convertere, ad eamque quam libuerit temperiem, citra ullum instrumenti\n[[256.5]] damnum, reducere. </p>\n<p> [[256.6]] Grandamici Experimentum a Te recitatum, fidei adeo sublestae habetur a Nostratibus, ut\n[[256.7]] neminem hactenus repererim, qui dignum judicet, cui peragendo tempus impendatur. </p>\n<p> [[256.8]] Certum est, quod Monconisius de pulvere Küfleriano, ingentes naves duorum triumve\n[[256.9]] minutorum spatio in fundum agente, commemorat; revera enim id praestitum fuit, imperante\n[[256.10]] Cromwello, qui et in eo erat, ut cum Inventore de certo precio contraheret; morte tamen rei\n[[256.11]] executionem praeoccupante. </p>\n<p> [[256.12]] Compos fieri non possum libri a te desiderati, cui titulus, <i>Gabriel Plat de thesauris\n[[256.13]] subterraneis</i>: Interim edocuit me vir Philosophus et in Chymicis versatissimus, qui eum totum\n[[256.14]] evolvit expenditque, nullam ea in re, quam Tu indigitas, transmutationem intercedere, sed totum\n[[256.15]] negotium in eo consistere, quod Aurum ex Antimonio parva quantitate, perinde atque ex Ferro,\n[[256.16]] elici sive extrahi possit. </p>\n<p> [[256.17]] Experimentum Becheri impressum, de methodo scil. ferrum ex limo lateritio et lini oleo\n[[256.18]] parandi, in oras nostras pervenit, et jam modo sub examine versatur; cujus eventum suo\n[[256.19]] tempore perscribam. </p>\n<p> [[256.20]] Vidisti sine dubio, quae Cassinus nuper de Maculis in Sole, Augusto novissimo observatis\n[[256.21]] commentatus est; quaeque de eodem argumento <i>Ephemeridibus</i> meis <i>Philosophicis</i>, N^#'o 74.\n[[256.22]] eodem mense evulgatis, annotavimus. Non dubium, quin et Tu eas inspexeris; uti eaedem et\n[[256.23]] Amstelodami, Hamburgi, et Londini observatae fuerunt. </p>\n<p> [[256.24]] Clariss^#'u^#'s Wallisius tertium et ultimum volumen edidit operis sui <i>de Motu et Mechanice</i>,\n[[256.25]] ubi, inter complura alia, tractat de quinque Potentiis Mechanicis, ad motum facilitandum\n[[256.26]] comparatis, de Vecte scilicet, Axi in Peritrochio, Trochlea, Cochlea, et Cuneo; deque aliis, quae\n[[256.27]] ad has reduci possunt. Inserit non-nulla de Hydrostaticis; de Gravitate et Elatere Aëris, deque\n[[256.28]] Atmosphaerae contrapondio; unde ea derivat effecta, quae Naturae a vacuo abhorrentiae philosophorum\n[[256.29]] vulgus attribuit; addita complurium Experimenti Torricelliani phaenomenum\n[[256.30]] Explicatione; multarumque Quaestionum Mechanicarum Solutione etc. </p>\n<p> [[257.1]] Exemplaria ejus quamprimum sine dubio Hamburgum transvehentur; unde brevi poterunt\n[[257.2]] Moguntiam curari. </p>\n<p> [[257.3]] Telescopia et Microscopia Anglica quod attinet, scire Te velim, Artificem hic esse unum\n[[257.4]] alterumve, qui talia elaborent, quae hactenus Nostratium non modo, sed et Advenarum atque\n[[257.5]] Extraneorum applausum meruerint. Arduum nonnihil est, quid ea praestent, examussim designare.\n[[257.6]] Dn. Hevelius non ita dudum Telescopium 50 pedum, triginta libris sterling; nec non\n[[257.7]] Microscopium eximiae magnitudinis et praestantiae, decem libris sterl. a nobis procuravit;\n[[257.8]] mihique nuper scripsit, utroque sibi abunde satisfactum. Ni fallor, Telescopium 60 pedes\n[[257.9]] longum, probe elaboratum, statuitur amplificare objectum 1 000 000^#'e^#'s: Et Microscopium, quale\n[[257.10]] supra dixi, tantundem. Specula concava Ustoria quod spectat, Artificum nostrorum unus offert,\n[[257.11]] velle se, precio 10 librarum Anglicarum, tale speculum conficere, cujus diameter sit 16 pollicum,\n[[257.12]] quodque ad duorum pedum distantiam urat efficaciter. Nosti, in Gallia jam quid amplius\n[[257.13]] fuisse praestitum. Forte et nostri homines majora praestarent, si consimili praemio stimularentur.\n[[257.14]] Hisce vale, meque virtutis ac doctrinae tuae Cultoribus accense. </p>\n<p> [[257.15]] Dab. Londini d. 28. Septemb. 1671. </p>\n",
  "number": "81.",
  "title": "HEINRICH OLDENBURG AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "London, 28. September (8. Oktober) 1671. [73.86.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:81. HEINRICH OLDENBURG AN LEIBNIZ London, 28. September (8. Oktober) 1671. [73.86.] Ampliss^#'o et Consultiss^#'o Viro Dⁿ^#'o Goth. Guil. Leibnitio J.U.D. et Consil. Moguntino Henr. Oldenburg Sal. Tardius aliquanto binis tuis novissimis, 18. junii et 20. ejusdem ad me datis, respondeo, quod rusticar...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>